# lab.surface: fluid nets in the lab (V1: pipes and pipe-to-ground as route carriers), on the
# fluids worker's region of the lab surface (x 740..860, y 400..560; the surface is 2048x2048,
# x and y from -1024 to 1023). The lab rules: free materials, direct building. The two claims
# are the offshore pumps' water: lab ground has none, so tools/lab_fluids.py sets their tiles to
# water before the apply, and nothing (a bridge pole) is ever planned on them.
surface  lab
mode     lab
terrain  none
catalog  base

place steam  = steam  plot 780,452 20x24
place sulfur = sulfur plot 810,455 20x16

claim lake-steam box 774,464 780,475 "water for the steam pump (lab: set_tiles)"
claim lake-sulfur box 820,448 829,455 "water for the sulfur pump (lab: set_tiles)"
